{
  "title": "test_pretool_hook_config fails when the working tree has \
uncommitted pipeline output",
  "description": "tests/test_pretool_hook_config.py::test_blocks_github_issues_and_raw_pr_publication \
runs the real .claude/hooks/agent-issues-pretool-hook.sh and asserts that \
blocking 'git push origin HEAD' mentions 'agent-submit'. But the hook checks \
the actual repo working tree first: if data/pipeline-snapshots or \
data/pipeline-runs have uncommitted modifications, it emits the 'Refusing to \
publish while generated output is modified' message instead, and the assertion \
fails.\n\
\n\
So `make test` fails in any worktree where `make pipeline` output hasn't been \
committed yet — which is a normal intermediate state during extraction work \
(observed 2026-07-02 while working on core-shared-html-text-cleanup).\n\
\n\
The test should isolate the hook from repo state, e.g. run it in a scratch git \
repo fixture or stub the generated-output check, so it exercises the \
command-blocking logic deterministically.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "agent-issues",
    "tests",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-02T20:30:00-07:00",
